/-!
# VIII09 — the actual ε³ `ell` bridge

Along the test family the frozen angular functional

  `ellFun f m N w p a R = (N²/(f m)) w' - 4 (N/f)(p' + w a') a`

is used through the corrected quantity `ellFun + 2 * ε * j`.
Multiplying this corrected quantity by the genuine denominators
`(1 + ε² u)(1 + ε² z)` gives a polynomial in `ε`.
The `ε`-linear coefficient of this corrected, denominator-cleared expression vanishes
(the first-order rotation relation), and its `ε³` coefficient is

  `R³ d' + 6c - R³(u+z) v_1' - 4 q₂ b_1`,

where `q₂ = Q u + R²(p₂' + v_1 b_1')` is the physical charge-drift combination, which the
accepted anchor identity `anchor_q` sends to `0`.  Hence the limit is `R³d' + 6c - r3_j(1/R)/R`.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 3000000

